The best fit position for RX J0720.4-3125, found by averaging the 0^{\\rm th} order data from the three HRC-S datasets, is (J2000) \\alpha=07^{\\rm h}20^{\\rm m}24\\fs 96, \\delta=-31\\arcdeg 25\\arcmin 49\\farcs 6, with rms uncertainty of \\approx 0\\farcs 6 in each coordinate due to _CXO_ aspect uncertainties. This is consistent (1\\farcs 4 away) with the optical position (Kulkarni & van Kerkwijk 1998). The X-ray source appears unresolved and its profile is consistent with that of a point source (half-power radius of \\approx 0\\farcs 5).

